Appendix A: Core Definitions and Notation

A.1 General Notation

· \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0} – non‑negative real numbers.
· \mathbb{N} – natural numbers \{0,1,2,\dots\}.
· For a finite set S, |S| denotes its cardinality.
· P – number of pipeline stages.
· M – number of training micro‑batches.
· \tau – base duration of a single compute operation (unit‑time model). In real‑time models we use T_{\text{comp}}, T_F, T_{BI}, T_{BW}, T_{\text{inf}}.

A.2 BG‑IR (Bare‑Graph Intermediate Representation)

Definition A.1 (BG‑IR).
G=(V,E,\tau,\delta,d,\kappa_V,\kappa_E,\sigma) where

· V: finite set of nodes,
· d:V\to\{1,\dots,P\}, stage assignment,
· \kappa_V:V\to\{\texttt{compute, send, recv, alloc, free}\},
· \tau:V\to\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0} duration (compute) or data volume (send/recv); \tau=0 for alloc/free,
· \sigma:V\to\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0} allocation size,
· E\subseteq V\times V edges,
· \kappa_E:E\to\{\texttt{data, gradient, memory, comm\_order}\},
· \delta:E\to\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0} minimum edge latency.

A forward BG‑IR is acyclic and uses only \texttt{data} and \texttt{memory} edges.

Definition A.2 (Valid schedule). S:V\to\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0} is valid if:

1. Precedence: \forall (u,v)\in E,\; S(v) \ge S(u)+\tau(u)+\delta(u,v).
2. Device mutual exclusion: \forall u\neq v,\, d(u)=d(v), [S(u),S(u)+\tau(u))\cap[S(v),S(v)+\tau(v))=\emptyset.
3. Link buffer: \forall t and link (p,p+1), total in‑flight data \le B_{\text{link}}(p).
4. Memory: \forall t and stage p, total size of live tensors \le B_{\text{mem}}(p).

A.3 Cyclo‑Static Dataflow (CSDF)

A CSDF graph (Bilsen et al., 1996) is a pair (A,E) with actors A and edges E. Each actor a has period \varphi(a)\in\mathbb{N} and, for each incident edge, production/consumption sequences of length \varphi(a). A repetition vector q:A\to\mathbb{N}_{>0} exists iff balance equations hold. Consistency \Leftrightarrow existence of a live, bounded periodic schedule.

